---
import TradeAnalyzer from '../../components/TradeAnalyzer';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Trade"
  description="Evaluate a trade: what each side is worth for the rest of the season under your league's scoring, how your team changes category by category, and a verdict."
>
  <section>
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Trade</h1>
    <p class="mt-1 max-w-3xl text-sm text-muted">
      Pick the players each side gives. Each is valued above a replacement-level player under your league's scoring,
      over the games they are expected to play from today, so an injured star and a two-for-one are judged on the same
      scale. With your league's rosters set up, you also see your team's categories and ranks before and after, and
      picking a player to get (or give) suggests the packages from the other roster that make the trade about even.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <TradeAnalyzer client:only="react" />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
